    {
      "id": "sol.amc-8-2005-p19.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "Drop the altitude from \\(C\\) to meet \\(\\overline{AD}\\) at \\(F\\). The existing altitude from \\(B\\) meets \\(\\overline{AD}\\) at \\(E\\).\n\nBy the Pythagorean theorem, \\(AE=\\sqrt{30^2-24^2}=18\\) and \\(FD=\\sqrt{25^2-24^2}=7\\). Also \\(EF=BC=50\\).\n\nThus \\(AD=18+50+7=75\\), and the trapezoid perimeter is \\(30+50+25+75=180\\).\n\nThus, A is the correct answer.",
      "hints": [
        "Drop perpendiculars to split the trapezoid into right triangles and a rectangle.",
        "Use the \\(18-24-30\\) and \\(7-24-25\\) right triangles."
      ],
